---
description: Enforces modern Java 21+ and Spring Boot 3 idiomatic standards.
globs: ["**/*.java", "**/pom.xml", "**/application*.yml"]
alwaysApply: false
---
# 🎯 Java Spring Boot 3 Standards

Enforce modern Java 21+ and Spring Boot 3 idiomatic standards.

## Rules
- ALWAYS use Records for immutable DTOs (not POJOs with getters/setters).
- ALWAYS use Pattern Matching for `switch` and `instanceof` (Java 21+).
- ALWAYS use Constructor injection via `@RequiredArgsConstructor` or explicit constructors.
- NEVER use `@Autowired` on private fields.
- ALWAYS use `jakarta.*` namespace exclusively (ban `javax.*`).
- ALWAYS use RFC 7807 Problem Details for REST error handling via `@ControllerAdvice` + `ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail()`.
- ALWAYS use Virtual Threads for I/O-bound tasks (`Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`).
- ALWAYS use Sealed interfaces for domain hierarchies.
- ALWAYS use `Optional` return types for nullable queries.
- NEVER return null from service methods.
- ALWAYS use `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` for read-only operations.
- ALWAYS use `List.of()`, `Map.of()`, `Set.of()` for immutable collections.
- ALWAYS use Text blocks (`"""`) for multi-line strings.
- NEVER catch generic `Exception` — catch specific exceptions.
- NEVER use `@SuppressWarnings` without justification comment.

## Verification
- Run `mvn test-compile` to ensure compilation.
- Run `mvn test` to ensure tests pass.
- Check for any `javax.*` imports.
